From 224bdef46b9586b3d2800cc5da8139e31c1c475b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 10:17:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: fix MLO per-link STA metrics and MLD data model
 tracking

Per-link metrics for MLO clients were wrong at every stage of the path, and
the resulting absence of a valid per-link SNR left steering permanently
blocked with "no SNR measurement".

- nl80211: NL80211_ATTR_MAC is not a dump-side filter, so a GET_STATION dump
  returns every station on the netdev. get_sta_info() overwrote sta_info on
  each message and returned whichever station came last in the dump, so all
  links of all MLDs resolved to the same station. Match the requested MAC and
  return false when it is absent, so callers emit RCPI=220 ("not measured")
  rather than a borrowed reading.

- agent: the station table is keyed by MLD MAC only, with the per-link
  breakdown nested under NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS, so per-link queries by
  affiliated-link MAC never matched. Key the query by MLD MAC and keep
  passing the per-link interface name, whose encoded link ID selects the
  nested block.

- agent: TLV 0xa2 summed every per-monitor report of the same MLD MAC, but
  each monitor reports the MLD-wide aggregate, multiplying every counter by
  the affiliated-link count. Dedup per query round instead, with the state
  spanning all handle_ap_metrics_response() calls in the round rather than
  only the BSS iterations within one call.

- agent: the legacy branch of process_client_association() erased the
  associated_sta_mlds entry, so an MLO client reclassified as SLO lost its
  MLD tracking and TLV 0x96 fell back to aggregate emission. Add
  erase_mlo_entry to AgentDB::erase_client(), defaulting to true, and pass
  false there.

- agent: m_radio_mac is overwritten with the AP MLD MAC on MLO "_link<N>"
  monitor interfaces, but radio_uid must always be the physical radio MAC.
  Keep it in m_physical_radio_mac for the Metric Reporting Policy gate and
  Profile-2 Radio Metrics.

- controller: a STAMLD instance was only pruned when the Topology Response
  carried an AssociatedStaMldConfigurationReport, which an agent the client
  has roamed away from never sends, leaving a stale duplicate under the
  previous agent. Drop registrations held under a different AP MLD before
  creating the live instance, and reconcile on every Topology Response,
  pruning only STA MLDs the database independently agrees have left.

- controller: STAMLD_ADDED fired only for newly-created instances, so a STA
  steering back to a previously-visited AP reused the instance and left
  qmesh-lib's path DB stale, blocking the per-link SNR getter. Fire it
  unconditionally; db_add_sta_mld() updates in place and is idempotent.

- controller: dm_set_sta_link_metrics() resolved the radio via
  get_radio_by_bssid(), which fails for an AP MLD MAC since that is never
  registered as a standalone BSS. Fall back to matching the MLD MAC against
  each agent's ap_mlds and resolving the radio from the first affiliated AP.

Debug logging on this path is retained deliberately while it is still under
investigation.

Signed-off-by: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
